WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.149
The Battle of Wakanda in ​Avengers: Infinity
War was an event that will reverberate throughout

00:00:05.149 --> 00:00:10.250
the MCU for years, and in one of its climactic
moments, two of the Avengers'​ biggest guns

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.420
failed to come through.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.640
Fans have wondered ever since: how did Thanos
defeat Vision and Scarlet Witch so easily?

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.980
"I thought you were formidable, machine.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.380
But you're dying, like any man."

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:29.580
The question was answered by Avengers: Infinity
War and Avengers: Endgame directors Joe and

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:33.900
Anthony Russo during a Twitter Q&amp;A they conducted
for Wired's Tech Support series.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.851
Essentially, they, along with screenwriters
Christopher Markus and Stephen McFeely, knew

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.780
that the pair would have to be hobbled if
Thanos were to achieve his victory.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.239
Vision's injury early on in the film was the
circumstance which allowed the Mad Titan to

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.800
narrowly avoid a whipping at the hands of
the two heroes.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.360
Joe Russo explained:

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:58.520
"Vision gets skewered right at the very beginning
of that fight, so he's really not functioning

00:00:58.520 --> 00:00:59.420
at full power."

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:03.900
He went on to say that Vision even becomes,
quote, "a liability in the fight," putting

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.360
Scarlet Witch at a disadvantage since she
has to protect him.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:11.180
Anthony Russo chimed in to add this comment
about Corvus Glaive's sword:

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:15.780
"And as Vision mentions, that weapon had an
effect on him that he didn't expect."

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.730
Joe added that with Wanda and Vision cornered,
it takes the combined might of Captain America,

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.250
Falcon and Black Widow to get them out of
the jam.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:27.360
Apparently, that early battle weakened Vision
enough that Wanda was forced to destroy the

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.250
Mind Stone mounted in Vision's forehead to
stop Thanos.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:34.150
Of course, that only stopped Thanos for a
moment, since the Mad Titan used the Time

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:38.700
Stone to undo her action, and ripped the Mind
Stone from Vision's head himself, killing

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.420
him yet again.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:43.700
With the final piece of the Infinity Gauntlet
in place, Thanos unleashed the snap heard

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.300
'round the universe, reducing Wanda and a
slew of other heroes to dust.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:52.460
The Russo brothers previously clarified shortly
after Infinity War's release that, since they

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:56.970
knew that the Mind Stone-powered Vision would
be a primary target of Thanos and his Black

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:59.500
Order, it was necessary to render him vulnerable.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.900
It just so happened that Glaive's attack on
Vision might have been the deciding factor

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.560
in the Mad Titan's ultimate victory.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:09.740
Fortunately, as we all know, Thanos' victory
was eventually reversed during the events

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:14.440
of Endgame by a Stark Gauntlet-wielding Bruce
Banner after the Avengers' successful mission

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:15.140
through time.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.520
Scarlet Witch, along with all of the other
dusted heroes, was revived, but Vision was

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.060
not, since he didn't die from the first snap.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.540
This raises the question of how the character
will return for the upcoming Disney+ limited

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:31.560
series Wandavision, and while we don't know
for sure, we can hazard a pretty good guess.

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:36.020
It's been speculated that Wanda will use her
growing reality-warping powers to create a

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:40.710
nice little alternate universe, one in which
Vision is still alive and that this action

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.340
might lead to some serious trouble.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.660
We learned from the events of Avengers: Endgame
that alternate timelines and realities are

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.740
not things which one should tamper with lightly.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:53.520
If Wanda's abilities evolve to be consistent
with her powers in the comics, her meddling

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.860
might end up causing serious problems.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.120
Those problems might require a doctor's assistance.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.080
It's already been announced that the events
of WandaVision will tie directly into Doctor

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:06.080
Strange sequel, Doctor Strange in the Multiverse
of Madness.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.240
All things considered, we appear to be looking
at one heck of a double-edged sword.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.420
On the one hand, everyone loves Vision, and
he's coming back.

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:18.240
On the other, his return will almost certainly
lead to a massive threat to all of existence.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.980
We suppose you've got to take the bad with
the good.

